<section xml:id="sec-what-is-a-function" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>What is a Function?</title>

	<objectives>
		<introduction>
			<p>
				In this section, we learn how to:
			</p>
		</introduction>
		<ol>
			<li><p>Articulate the definition of a function, and the connection between each input's output.</p></li>
			<li><p>Identify the domain and range of a function.</p></li>
			<li><p>Represent functions in various ways, including tables, graphs, and equations.</p></li>
    </ol>
	</objectives>

  <subsection>
    <title>Applications</title>

    <p>
      Intro:
      <ol>
        <li>
          <p>
            A consulting firm changes a flat fee of <m>\$500</m> plus <m>\$50</m> per hour for a project,
            plus <m>\$350</m> for each consultant who works on the project.
            If <m>h</m> represents the number of hours worked and <m>c</m> represents the number of consultants hired,
            describe a formula for the total charge for a project.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p>
            Text
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </p>

    <example>
      <statement>
        <p>
          Solve the equation <m>3x+1 = 9</m>
        </p>
      </statement>
      <answer>
        <p>
          First, we subtract <m>1</m> from both sides to get <m>3x = 8</m>.
          Next, we divide both sides by <m>3</m> to get <m>x = \frac{8}{3}</m>.
        </p>
      </answer>
    </example>

  </subsection>

